<!--BlockML Core — fix expression errors how-to

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.howto.FixExpressionErrors-->
<howto:FixExpressionErrors xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:diag="org.blockml.bml.diagnostic"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation"
  xmlns:howto="org.blockml.bml.documentation.howto"
  xmlns:meta="org.blockml.bml.meta">

  <baseType>
    howto:HowTo
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A how-to for fixing expression errors
  </is>
  <summary>
    Resolve ${ }, interpolated Text, and &lt;$ $> expression diagnostics — syntax,
    unknown refs, type/payload mismatches, Restricted Profile, linking, and model context.
  </summary>
  <documentation>
    Procedure when an expression-related BML_EXPR_* (or embed) diagnostic is reported:
    1. Confirm host context — whole-value member ${ } vs interpolated Text holes vs implementation
       &lt;$ $> (doc:Expressions, doc:EmbeddedExpressions).
    2. Interpolation holes — Restricted Profile only (property access, literals, +, #strings.*,
       #math.*). Not desugared to concatenation. @model / @bean / Capability calls / each-with
       variables → BML_EXPR_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_INTERPOLATION. Unclosed ${ → BML_EXPR_SYNTAX_ERROR.
       Interpolation on a non-Text member → BML_EXPR_TYPE_MISMATCH. this without # is a member
       (#this.this), not the instance.
    3. Syntax errors — check delimiters, quotes, operators; embeds must not nest &lt;$ $>.
    4. Unknown property — verify member exists in scope; StructType fields by name only (not [0]).
    5. Unknown bean / builtin — declare bml:bean Aggregation or use a V1 #built-in.
    6. Type / payload mismatch — align expression result with member type; map call args via
       FunctionMapping (doc:FunctionMappingModel).
    7. Linking (@bean.capa without parens) — source Outbound, target Inbound, compatible payloads.
    8. Relative @model: — ensure a parent Aggregation established binding context.
    9. V1 — avoid deferred @bean execution / model / linking features until implemented.
  </documentation>
  <keywords>
    <meta:Keyword value="expression" />
    <meta:Keyword value="interpolation" />
    <meta:Keyword value="BML_EXPR_SYNTAX_ERROR" />
    <meta:Keyword value="BML_EXPR_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_INTERPOLATION" />
    <meta:Keyword value="bean" />
    <meta:Keyword value="built-in" />
    <meta:Keyword value="embedded" />
  </keywords>
  <references>
    <see type="doc:Expressions" relation="HowToStep">
      Step 1 — ${ } language, #this, interpolation, V1 support.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:EmbeddedExpressions" relation="HowToStep">
      Step 2 — implementation embeds and delimiter rules.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:FunctionMappingModel" relation="HowToStep">
      Step 3 — call argument mapping diagnostics.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:BmlDirectives" relation="HowToStep">
      Step 4 — each/with variable scopes.
    </see>
    <see type="diag:BML_EXPR_SYNTAX_ERROR" relation="SeeAlso">
      Parse failure diagnostic.
    </see>
    <see type="diag:BML_EXPR_UNKNOWN_PROPERTY" relation="SeeAlso">
      Unknown property / invalid struct index access.
    </see>
    <see type="diag:BML_EXPR_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_INTERPOLATION" relation="SeeAlso">
      Restricted Profile violation in an interpolation hole.
    </see>
  </references>
</howto:FixExpressionErrors>
